th":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-99.1/state.json","size_bytes":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-99.1","local_name":"sase-99.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-99","agent_clan_generation":"20260725084125","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-99.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-99[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]NEIGHBORS section for agent lane metadata panels[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every agent lane metadata panel (family container rows, and single [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]agents that own their lane) renders a numbered, fold-aware [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]NEIGHBORS section listing exactly the related agents the `~` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]neighbors modal offers for that lane, digit keys jump to (or [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]revive) them, and single agents gain real fold-level support.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase/repos/plans/202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]lane_neighbors_section.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Lane identity, lane fold scale, and the shared neighbor [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]projection[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]lane-model[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase lane-model' section: add `agent_owns_lane`, a lane fold scale [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]helper, and a pure `AgentLaneNeighborProjection` builder, then refactor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the `~` neighbors modal to build its choices from that same projection [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]so the panel section and the modal can never drift.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared roster numbering, group labels, and entry limits[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]roster-shared[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase roster-shared' section: extend the shared numbered member-roster [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]renderer with a document-wide digit allocator, per-entry group labels, a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fold-driven entry limit, dismissed-row styling, target roles, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]jump-map merging, leaving every existing roster byte-identical.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]NEIGHBORS section rendering and lane panel wiring[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]neighbors-render[dim] · [dim][/dim]after lane-model, roster-shared[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase neighbors-render' section: render the NEIGHBORS section as the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]last metadata-region section of every lane panel, wire the lane fold [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]level through `build_header_text` for single agents, and publish one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]merged member-jump map per lane document.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Digit jump, revive, footer, and help for lane neighbors[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]lane-jump[dim] · [dim][/dim]after neighbors-render[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase lane-jump' section: extend digit-key member jump to lane [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]containers and neighbor/dismissed target roles, revive dismissed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]neighbors, replace the stale regular-agent fold notification, and update[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the footer and help modal.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fold contracts, visual snapshots, docs, and full check[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF8